course: dictionary
lesson: 12540
title: Detecting: noticing what is hidden
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Detecting is the -ing form of detect. To detect something is to notice or find it when it is hard to see, hear or find. «The smoke alarm is detecting smoke in the kitchen.» The alarm is sensing the smoke so that it can warn us.
explain: The word can also mean searching for things with a special tool. «Sam spent the afternoon metal detecting on the beach.» Metal detecting means using a machine that beeps when it finds metal under the sand.
explain: Use context to check your meaning. Ask what the words around detecting tell you. If someone is using a machine to search, or is looking for clues, then detecting means finding something hidden. Try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Detecting is the -ing form of the verb detect: detect, detects, detected, detecting.
fact: «Detecting» can mean noticing something that is hard to see, hear or find.
fact: Metal detecting is a hobby where people use a machine to find metal objects, often on beaches.
fact: A smoke alarm is a device for detecting smoke.
fact: Detectives detect clues to solve a mystery.
exercise: «The smoke alarm is detecting smoke in the kitchen.» What is the alarm doing? | *Sensing smoke so that it can give a warning | Painting the walls | Cooking the dinner | Making the kitchen hot
exercise: Sam went metal detecting on the beach. What was he doing? | Swimming in the sea | *Using a machine to search for hidden metal | Building a sandcastle
exercise: Which word is the -ing form of detect? | Detect | Detected | *Detecting | Detects
test: «The detective is detecting clues to solve the mystery.» What does detecting mean here? | Forgetting the clues | Throwing the clues away | Hiding the clues | *Finding and noticing hidden clues
test: In «Metal detecting is fun on a sunny day», what is detecting? | A kind of fish | A type of cloud | *A hobby of searching with a machine | A loud noise
exam: Which sentence shows detecting meaning noticing something that is hard to hear? | «The bus is late again.» | «The rain is falling on the roof.» | *«The dog is detecting a faint sound from far away.» | «The cat is sleeping by the fire.»
